 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "HOLD_WHILE is not form-dependent in the code (no decidingForms), although the brief lists 들고 among the deciding forms; the 30% share therefore has to come from PLACE_REL, PLACE_ON_PATTERN, GIVE, TRADE and ordered SEQUENCE.",
  "DEFEAT_ENTITY with count 1 prints 한 마리, and 하나 is a young word for the coverage lexicon for a long time; count 2 (두 마리) avoids it. Removing old count-1 steps made 하나 young again for a later L3 sentence (adv_adventure_arbalistic/s2), which I paid back with a 한 개 in a finale line.",
  "The coverage lexicon reads 파세요 (sell) as 파다 (dig) and 사세요 as 사다; both verbs are young for everyone before the village trails, so every TRADE step costs one unknown word besides its object. Also 쓰다, 입다, 신다 (EQUIP) and 나가다/들어가다 (TRANSIT) are young verbs, so an EQUIP or SEQUENCE step with a new item has two unknown words.",
  "There is no shoot or brush goal: ol_betsy (shoot a crossbow) is a crafted crossbow, an arrow and a night fight, and brush_armadillo cannot say that the brush is used on the armadillo (the scute is just acquired).",
  "PLACE_ON_PATTERN: BEHIND does not fit a WALL (validator), and a creature without a Korean name in the anchor list (armadillo) cannot be an anchor of PLACE_REL.",
  "The (verb, object) pair limit already blocks PLACE torch, lantern, chest, ladder, jack_o_lantern, carved_pumpkin, STACK cobblestone/stone_bricks/spruce_planks/oak_planks, EAT pumpkin_pie and SPREAD white_carpet; I used other ids (colour carpets, orange bed, cyan candle, mangrove sign, granite, sandstone). Rings are the most used pattern (31); wall, cross and stairs are nearly unused and carry the novelty score.",
  "Step signatures ignore the count and the material of a pillar size only through the size, so CRAFT compass / note block / smithing table collide with earlier trails (abenteuerpfad, musikpfad, schmiedepfad); a trail on the learner path before them counts as the duplicate even if the older trail is not mine.",
  "Words in the old finale lines were carrying encounters: dropping them cost seenShare (죽다 only occurred in 숨을 죽였어요) and made 여덟, 늑대, 뼈 and 하나 young for later trails. I put 죽었어요, 늑대, 뼈 and 여덟 into the finale lines on purpose; a new batch can lose such encounters unnoticed.",
  "The English/German giveaway check refuses 'then' and the order words for ordered SEQUENCE; the translations have to be vague ('in the order the Korean says').",
  "The unknown-word budget is global and path-dependent: a sentence with two new words (a new item name next to a new place or creature) cannot be avoided in a five-step trail, so each new multiword item name (대장장이 작업대, 조각된 석재 벽돌, 아르마딜로 인갑) needs its own step before it can sit next to another new word."
 ],
 "openIssues": [
  "Reachability inside week one: the lightning rod needs three copper ingots (a copper vein) and the finale needs rain; the crossbow needs iron, string and a tripwire hook; the brush needs copper, a feather and a stick; the lodestone needs eight chiseled stone bricks and an iron ingot (the 26.3 recipe is iron, not netherite); the savanna may be far from spawn; the pillager patrol is random and dangerous (two pillagers by day with a crossbow, a shield and a granite wall).",
  "TRADE steps need a farmer who buys potatoes and, after a few trades, sells pumpkin pies (apprentice level); a village without a farmer cannot finish adv_adventure_salvage_sherd.",
  "The vanilla advancement names are gone from avoid_vibration, heart_transplanter, minecraft_trials_edition, salvage_sherd and trim_with_any_armor_pattern (new Korean, English and German titles). They are proposed for level 3 (see proposedForLevel3); I did not change any koreanLevel.",
  "adv_adventure_voluntary_exile keeps its title but is a softer path: the vanilla advancement kills a raid captain; here the player defeats two pillagers with a crossbow in daylight. It could move to level 3 with the real captain fight.",
  "unknownOverOneShare is 0.0490 (start 0.0503, phase0 after wave 9 0.0509); the one sentence of mine with two unknown words is brush_armadillo/s4 (아르마딜로에게 거미 눈을 주세요).",
